@@ -87,3 +87,26 @@ From the second month on, none of this is needed.
 1. Open Claude Code in this repository and say what you want, naming the rule from [RULES.md](RULES.md) — e.g. *"Change rule 5.4 so 'wholesale' tags go to a Wholesale channel."*
 2. Claude Code updates the rules, the code and the tests, runs the tests, and regenerates `dist/DairyPill_EOM.gs`.
 3. Copy the new `dist/DairyPill_EOM.gs` into Apps Script again (select all in `Code.gs`, paste, then put your folder ID back in), save, and run.
+   If Claude Code says `appsscript.json` changed too, paste that as well (see F.1 step 2). Pasting new code updates the Studio steps by itself; you don't need to install again.
+
+## F. Starting it from Workspace Studio (no script editor)
+
+Instead of choosing **buildEOM** → **Run**, you can run a Studio flow: type the month, click run, and get an email with the link (or the problem) a few minutes later. Your Workspace admin has to allow custom steps first: Admin console → Apps → Google Workspace → Workspace Studio → Custom steps settings → **ON**, with **Allow unpublished (test) custom steps** ticked.
+
+### F.1 One-time: install the steps (about 5 minutes)
+1. In the Apps Script project, paste the latest [`dist/DairyPill_EOM.gs`](dist/DairyPill_EOM.gs) into `Code.gs` as usual. Keep your folder ID.
+2. Click the **gear icon (Project Settings)** and tick **Show "appsscript.json" manifest file in editor**. Go back to the editor (`< >` icon), open **appsscript.json**, select everything, and paste the contents of [`appsscript.json`](appsscript.json) from this repository. Press **Ctrl+S** (Cmd+S on Mac).
+3. Click **Deploy → Test deployments**. If it asks for a type, choose **Google Workspace Add-on**. Click **Install**, then **Done**.
+
+### F.2 One-time: build the flow
+1. Open Workspace Studio (Drive → the **EOM Reports** folder's menu → **Set up an automation** → **Do more in Studio**) and start a new flow.
+2. **Starter:** **Start manually**. Add one input called **Month** (text).
+3. **Step:** search for **Build DairyPill EOM** (it may be under add-ons or custom steps). In its **Month** box, insert the starter's **Month** variable.
+4. Name the flow **Build DairyPill EOM** and save or turn it on. The first time, Google asks for permission. The new permissions are "send email as you" (the result email, which only goes to you) and "run when you're not present" (the background build).
+5. Optional: do the same with the **Build DairyPill Shopify Sell Thru** step for a second flow.
+
+### F.3 Every month
+1. Put the reports in the month folder (section B).
+2. Run the **Build DairyPill EOM** flow and type the month, e.g. `October 2026` (leave blank for last month).
+3. If something is missing, the flow's **Activity** shows the problem in plain English straight away. Otherwise you get an email within about 5 minutes with the workbook link (or the problem, if the full build stopped). Only one build runs at a time.
+4. After filling in the yellow tabs, run the flow again, the same as running **buildEOM** again.
